<article class="env-corollary" id="05TQ">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05TQ">Corollary <span data-tag="05TQ">7.7.2.12</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category which admits pullbacks and let $K$ be a simplicial set. If $K$-indexed colimits in $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ are universal, then the restriction functor </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Fun}( K^{\triangleright }, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})^{\operatorname{Cart}}_{/F} \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}( K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})^{\operatorname{Cart}}_{/F|_{K}} \]
</div>
<p> is is fully faithful for every colimit diagram $F: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. The converse holds if $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ admits $K$-indexed colimits or has a final object. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Theorem <a data-tag="05TL" href="/tag/05TL">7.7.2.8</a> with Remark <a data-tag="05TP" href="/tag/05TP">7.7.2.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
